PLAYWRIGHT + CUCUMBER BDD FRAMEWORK
A highly structured, practice-based test automation framework engineered with Playwright and Cucumber BDD using modern JavaScript (ES Modules) syntax.

FRAMEWORK SCOPE
This repository is a learning-focused implementation dedicated to isolating and mastering complex UI interaction paradigms, event handling, and custom framework architecture. It is designed to bridge the gap between basic script writing and enterprise-grade automation foundations.

TECH STACK & KEY INTEGRATIONS
Playwright: High-performance, cross-browser engine for modern web automation.

Cucumber BDD: Gherkin-driven workflow bridging readable business requirements and test step definitions.

JavaScript (ESM): Utilizes native ECMAScript Modules (import/export) for modern, modular clean code syntax.

Winston: Centralized asynchronous enterprise logging framework with strict severity handling.

Cucumber HTML Reporter: Auto-generated, interactive dashboard reporting with automated runtime artifact binding.

ARCHITECTURE & DIRECTORY LAYOUT
cucumber.js: Global Cucumber-JS runner profile configurations

generate-report.js: Post-execution parsing script for visual HTML dashboards

package.json: Framework dependencies and core npm script shortcuts

features/
--- dropdown.feature
--- radio-checkbox.feature

step-definitions/
--- common-steps.js
--- radio-checkbox-steps.js

utils/
--- hooks.js (Global execution lifecycle control)
--- logger.js (Winston logging service instance)
--- screenshotHelper.js (Visual capture pipeline for runtime failures)

CORE INFRASTRUCTURE FEATURES
On-Failure Screenshot Pipeline (AfterStep Hook)

Precision Tracking: Instantly snapshots the browser view state at the exact moment a step throws an error.

Report Embedding: Automatically encodes binary viewport arrays directly to the local JSON schema, nesting the visual proof right inside the failing Gherkin step block on the HTML dashboard.

Asynchronous Enterprise Logging (Winston Engine)

System Timestamps: High-fidelity microsecond tracking formatted as [YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss].

Severity Thresholding: Configured with a runtime barrier level (level: 'info'). It manages internal pipeline output verbosity automatically, tracking structural operational data (logger.info) and cascading system errors (logger.error) seamlessly across environments.

SETUP AND INSTALLATION
Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/GaneshRasal/Playwright-UI-Automation.git

Go into the project directory:
cd Playwright-UI-Automation

Install dependencies:
#npm install

Install managed Playwright browser binaries:
#npx playwright install

TEST EXECUTION ORCHESTRATION
Run the complete automated test suite:
#npm test

Isolate specific feature targets via Cucumber Tags:
npm run test -- --tags "@run-ai2"
#npx cucumber-js --tags "@input"
#npx cucumber-js --tags "@dropdown"
#npx cucumber-js --tags "@radio-checkbox"

Execute and synthesize visual HTML Dashboards:
#npm run test:report

EVALUATION REPORTS
Upon completing a test run utilizing the reporting pipeline, a styled interactive file is automatically populated at:

reports/html-report/index.html

Open this index path inside any modern web browser to view comprehensive failure logs, step analytics, and inline error screenshots.

